Jenkinsfile Explanation
Language Used
The Jenkinsfile is written in Groovy, which is the primary scripting language used for Jenkins pipelines. Groovy is a JVM-based language that combines features of Python, Ruby, and Smalltalk with Java-like syntax.

Line-by-Line Explanation
groovy
pipeline {
Declares a declarative pipeline (the modern way to define Jenkins pipelines)

groovy
    agent any
Specifies that the pipeline can run on any available agent (Jenkins worker node)

groovy
    tools {
        maven 'Maven 3.9.9'
        jdk 'JDK-21'
    }
Configures tools to be automatically installed and added to PATH:

Maven version 3.9.9

JDK version 21

groovy
    environment {
        DOCKER_CONFIG = "${env.WORKSPACE}/.docker"
        MINIKUBE_HOME = 'C:/minikube'
    }
Sets environment variables:

DOCKER_CONFIG: Path for Docker configuration

MINIKUBE_HOME: Location of Minikube installation

